# Air-Quality-Monitoring-System

A system that monitors deviation from a specific atmospheric condition using MQ-135 sensor and knowledge in Industrial Internet of Things and Additive Manufacturing applied. 
I stumbled upon this project I did years ago during my undergraduate years. I've always been afraid of gas explosive accident, very common in Nigeria. That curiosity of "How will I know if my gas is leaking....? 😄 " . I sat down with my close friend after a regular Mechatronics System Design class, he was interested and we started doing something about it. We started with arduino microcontroller but later changed to ESP32 after some frustration 🤣 . At last we achieved it. "3D Printed Casing, Gas Leakage detection system using ESP32 micro controller and GSM module" It will detect possible leaks of propane with MQ-135 sensor, switch on a red led bulb for visuals and send messages to your mobiles incase you are not around via the GSM module. If you are around it a buzzer will alert you straight away. All powered by a Lithium battery 18650 enclosed in a 3D printed casing. 
After expanding my knowledge in Industrial Internet of Things recently, I discovered beyond domestic application this can be employed in massive gas plants, and gas powered vehicles and in protecting high value infrastructure from possible gas explosion. 
